  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Correct order of bond dissociation enthalpy of halogens is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Due to inter electronic repulsions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> bond becomes weak and easily broken.</p><p>Bond dissociation energy of halogen family decreases down the group as the size of atom increases.</p>"
